  "notes": "Light for «حسنة» only; no motif on the Prophet ﷺ (79:13-15, 80). 80:9-12 «فما أرسلناك عليهم حفيظا» is not glossed (the only explanations are positive or Allah's first person «بعثناك/علينا»). 81:1-2 (their claimed «طاعة») not glossed as a fact. STAGING v4: 79: a man in the fields; the wheat grows on 79:4 (good; a wheat plate ending before the Name), the scene darkens briefly on 79:10 (hardship) and he lowers his head on 79:10 (from his own deeds); the darkness lifts before the Messenger is mentioned, so no hardship is tied to him (the fields are not withered). The man leaves on 79:12; 79:13-18 play on the empty fields (no lone figure while the sending of the Messenger is recited); the people come in on 80:1; the Prophet is never drawn and nobody bows or prostrates while he is named; 80 gets only camera moves (no gesture of obeying a person, no one turning toward an empty space). 81: the night street is empty while they say their word in his presence (81:1-3, not drawn); a party of them (only part: a small group) walks in on 81:4 after leaving and speaks on 81:7 and 81:11 (plotting by night, both tafsirs); wide shot on 81:17; geometric plate from 81:24, after the Name."
